144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The motivation behind CivicPulse is to address the lack of centralized and reliable information regarding everyday infrastructure disruptions experienced by local communities.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The major motivating factors are:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (1. Information Fragmentation : Infrastructure-related updates are scattered across multiple communication channels, making information difficult to access and verify.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (2. Lack of Real-Time Awareness : Residents often remain unaware of disruptions occurring in nearby localities until they personally experience them.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (3. Limited Incident Visibility : There is no consolidated geographical representation of reported infrastructure issues and their current status.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (4. Need for Community Participation :Residents can contribute valuable local information, but there is a lack of an organized mechanism to collect and validate such reports.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (5. Scalability and Reliability :A community information platform must support changing user demands, secure information management, and continuous availability.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
